  "instructions": [
    {
      "name": "burn_token",
      "docs": [
        "Burns tokens from the admin's token account, reducing total supply",
        "",
        "# Arguments",
        "* `ctx` - The context containing all required accounts for burning",
        "* `amount_normal_format` - The amount of tokens to burn in normal format (without decimals)",
        "e.g., 1000 = 1000 tokens (not 1000 base units)",
        "",
        "# Accounts",
        "* `admin` - The authorized admin account (must match ADMIN_PUBKEY), signer and authority",
        "* `admin_token_account` - The admin's associated token account to burn from",
        "* `ita_token_mint` - The mint account PDA that will have supply reduced",
        "* `token_program` - The SPL Token program",
        "",
        "# Returns",
        "* `Result<()>` - Ok(()) on success, or an error",
        "",
        "# Security",
        "* Only callable by the hardcoded ADMIN_PUBKEY",
        "* Amount must be greater than 0 (prevents unnecessary transactions)",
        "* Uses checked multiplication to prevent overflow attacks",
        "* Admin must have sufficient token balance to burn",
        "* Permanently reduces circulating supply (irreversible operation)",
        "",
        "# Notes",
        "* Amount is converted from normal format to base units (multiplied by 10^9)",
        "* Admin's token account must already exist and have sufficient balance",
        "* Burned tokens are permanently removed from circulation",
        "* No on-chain total supply tracking - admin manages supply manually",
        "* This is an irreversible operation - burned tokens cannot be recovered",
        "",
        "# Errors",
        "* `InvalidAmount` - If amount is 0",
        "* `AmountOverflow` - If decimal conversion causes overflow",
        "* Token program error - If insufficient balance in admin_token_account"
      ],
